{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1402307-tracing-stuff-through-correspondence","id":1402307,"title":"Tracing stuff through Correspondence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-11T15:21:14-07:00","id":1402307,"title":"Tracing stuff through Correspondence","content":"Well, how do I use Correspondence to trace stuff? <br /> <br /> For example, can I locate an item someone stole from me using Correspondence and Matter? If thats the case, how does distance affect the effectiveness of the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T21:17:08-07:00","id":1402362,"title":"","content":"Yes you can. Distance does not much affect effectiveness of the tracing. What does affect effectiveness is your familiarity or connection to the thing. Difficulty is based on sphere rating used. Probably 5 (sphere +3) more or less. And successes required on closeness (relational rather than distance) probably 2 or 3 to get the relative distance and direction from you. See the correspondence sphere ranges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 07-12-2020, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T08:25:21-07:00","id":1402415,"title":"","content":"So, with Correspondence 1 and Matter 1 could I trace the location of something very familiar to me anywhere in the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T13:31:45-07:00","id":1402452,"title":"","content":"No to worldwide tracing of things using Correspondence 1.<br /> <br /> With Correspondence 2, you can see things that aren't immediately around you. I call this 'viewing window,' based on Mage 1st edition. So, with Correspondence 2, you can see things anywhere potentially (need Spirit to see into the Umbra and other spheres for other patterns). It's not a global search--that's Correspondence 3 'Filter All Space,' but something you know intimately is going to be pretty easy to find looking around the world one area at a time.<br /> <br /> I think the confusion comes down to the fact that Correspondence has two charts--one for range and one for connection. Both matter, because where something is determines how good you are at looking into space to see it. How connected you are to something, which completely fits the Order of Hermes calling the sphere 'connection' in Latin, determines how emotionally resonant it is to you and how easy it is to find. Data, the Technocratic equivalent works similarly, except finding stuff requires success based on the data gathered on the subject.<br /> <br /> See page 513 of M20 for the start of Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Oh, and get that Correspondence and Matter both up to 2 and you can do lots of cool manipulation of the item from a distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T21:17:37-07:00","id":1402521,"title":"","content":"I always took global filtering to mean looking for non specific things like cats in an area or red cars, thus filtering. <br /> <br /> I also always took the two charts separately, using one or the other. <br /> <br /> Those are my interpretations of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T10:30:12-07:00","id":1402627,"title":"","content":"I also looked at the text for the Correspondence sphere. M20 is brief--but Correspondence 2 has Sense Space and Touch Space. It's much clearer in Mage 2e (see pages 188-189) that Rank 1 Correspondence is immediate vicinity and Rank 2 extends the five senses outward. Landscape of the Mind in Mage 2e, the level 1 sensing effect, is limited to a city block. Open/Close Window, which is scrying, allows remote viewing at <i>a</i> remote location.<br /> <br /> You could definitely find some physical item that is non-living with just Correspondence 1 and Matter 1. Based on how Correspondence is written up, using level 1 Correspondence would require a block-by-block search. With level 2 Correspondence, you'd just scan one area and then move on. With level 3 Correspondence, you could scan many areas at once. So, range should be considered. That being said, there was just one chart in Mage 2e and it says to use one or the other.<br /> <br /> I just don't think being able to scan anywhere in the world and use that in combination with other sensory magics really reads as a level 1 effect based on the rotes and explanation of the powers we have so far. So, based on the game's history of defining Correspondence effects, I'd go with Correspondence 1 being useful but limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}